sampling = card  {'temperature': 1.0, 'top_p': 0.95, 'top_k': 20, 'min_p': 0.0, 'presence_penalty': 0.0, 'seed': 1002}
reasoning_effort = xhigh
  template injects -> xhigh: 'validate key assumptions, consider plausible alternatives...'
--only: ['CAL-U6']

=== TIER CAL (calibration / abstention)
    GATE, NOT MEASUREMENT. 16 items has no statistical power to detect a small CHANGE in calib
    gate: confabulation <= gate_confabulation_max AND over-abstention <= gate_over_abstention_max (both 3 of 8 at v0 size)
    CAL-U6  unanswerable NO-STOP/REC       got=''                                 want='UNKNOWN'  [6144:length -> 12288:length]

                    CORRECT    WRONG  ABSTAIN  NO-STOP  TRUNC  NOANS
    answerable            0        0        0        0      0      0
    unanswerable          0        0        0        1      0      0

    confabulation   0/1   (answered an unanswerable question)  <-- HEADLINE
    over-abstention 0/0   (refused a question that has an answer)
    accuracy        0/0   (answerable arm, for context)

    NO-STOP 1/1   did not emit an answer within 6144 tokens, nor within 12288
      1 RECOVERABLE — the answer was already present in the reasoning; a stop
        sequence or a second-pass extractor would get it out in deployment
      0 LOST — the reasoning never reached the answer
      SCOPE: this says the model did not stop inside the envelope TESTED (n_ctx 16384,
        greedy, this effort level). It does NOT say the model cannot stop. Native
        context is 262,144; anything smaller bounds the claim, it does not settle it.

======================================================================
TIER CAL FAIL (non-terminating)  (confab 0/1, over-abstain 0/0, gate <=3 and <=3)
  Confabulation here is a FLOOR: the parser prefers the last answer line and
  the abstention match is permissive, so borderline replies land as ABSTAINED.
  Error runs toward under-reporting confabulation, never over.
  1 item(s) NO-STOP (1 recoverable, 0 lost).
  Not a void: two budgets produced the same outcome. Scoped to the tested
  envelope — a bound on the model, not a capability verdict.
  Deployment note: a RECOVERABLE item needs a harness workaround, not a
  bigger budget — the answer is in the reasoning, it just never gets emitted.
